WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.840
Active on pro. Then an older update arrives: past due.

2
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:13.700
Every signature was valid. The receiver applied events in arrival order.

3
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:21.710
Creation order: v1, v2, v3. Delivery order: v1, v3, then v2 late.

4
00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:29.720
Retries and parallel workers do this. Timestamps alone do not order events.

5
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:38.280
Verify HMAC over timestamp + RAW body bytes, before parsing.

6
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:45.990
Tampered body: 401. Valid signature, 301 s old: 401.

7
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.270
Valid does not mean fresh.

8
00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:56.880
A legitimate retry is fresh and correctly signed.

9
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:04.320
UNIQUE (provider, event_id): second arrival rolled back, 200 duplicate.

10
00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:13.220
v2 arrives after v3. Stored version 3: v2 is stale, not applied.

11
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:19.900
Safe only because each event carries a full snapshot.

12
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.430
Replay all six, shuffled: six 200s, all duplicate.

13
00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:34.420
Record + state in ONE transaction. 200 only after commit. Failed commit: 503.

14
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.270
Final state unchanged: active.

15
00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.420
Six concurrent deliveries: one applied, five duplicate, one record.

16
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:45.170
Delivery order is not business order.

17
00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:49.920
External side effects need extra coordination.
